Title: Nova Financial: Investment Analytics Dashboard

Description:
You are building an Investment Analytics Dashboard for a portfolio management app. The dashboard fetches market holding records, allows users to filter asset names, toggle between viewing asset classes, and change currency display preferences.

Sorting, filtering, and performing financial calculations over asset arrays can cause unnecessary re-renders. You must optimize the computed financial values using useMemo so that heavy calculations only re-run when relevant data changes—not when unrelated state (such as the display currency preference) updates.

Task Requirements:
Implement your solution inside the provided App.jsx file.

1. Data Fetching & Side Effects (useEffect)
Initial Data Load: On component mount, simulate fetching portfolio data using setTimeout. After exactly 600ms, populate the assets state with the provided MOCK_ASSETS array and set loading to false.

Document Title Update: Create a second useEffect that updates document.title to: "Portfolio - Total: ${formattedTotal}", where {formattedTotal} is the totalValue calculated from the current filtered assets list.

2. Optimized Computations (useMemo)
Implement a single useMemo hook to calculate an object returning { filteredAssets, totalValue }:

Filtering: Include assets where name matches searchTerm (case-insensitive) AND assetClass matches selectedCategory (if selectedCategory is "All", do not filter by category).

Total Value Calculation: Compute totalValue by summing quantity * currentPrice across all filtered assets.

Optimization Tracker: Inside your useMemo callback, you must include this exact line of code so the test suite can verify your optimization:

JavaScript
window.analyticsMemoCount = (window.analyticsMemoCount || 0) + 1;
Dependency Array: Ensure useMemo depends only on assets, searchTerm, and selectedCategory. Changing currency must not trigger useMemo.

3. Component Composition & Props Passing
<FilterBar/> Component: Pass searchTerm, setSearchTerm, selectedCategory, setSelectedCategory, currency, and setCurrency as props to this child component.

<PortfolioMetrics/> Component: Pass totalValue, currency, and assetCount (filteredAssets.length) as props.

<AssetTable/> Component: Pass filteredAssets as a prop named assets and currency as a prop named currency.
